course: dictionary
lesson: 3558
title: Fen: a word for wet land
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A fen is low, flat, wet land, a bit like a marsh, with reeds and peat. «The heron stood still among the reeds of the fen.» The clues are reeds and wet, so a fen is a damp place, not a dry field.
explain: The Fens are a large flat area in eastern England. Much of it was drained, which means the water was taken away, so farmers could grow crops there. A capital F means a place name, so the Fens is a special name for that region.
explain: Some words mean something different in another language. In an invented language called Selk, «fenmor» means a volcano, because fen means fire there and mor means mountain. That is not what fen means in English, so always check the meaning in the text you are reading.
fact: A fen is low, flat, wet land, like a marsh, often with reeds and peat.
fact: «Fen» is a noun: a fen, and more than one is fens.
fact: The Fens are a large, flat area of eastern England, and much of it has been drained for farming.
fact: History lessons talk about the Fens and about the draining of the Fens.
fact: In the made-up language Selk, fen means fire, so «fenmor» means volcano; in English, fen does not mean fire.
exercise: «The heron stood still among the reeds of the fen.» What is a fen? | A small shop in the town centre | *Low, flat, wet land with reeds | A fast train on a steel track | A tall mountain with snow on top
exercise: «The Fens are a large, flat area of eastern England.» Where are the Fens? | On the coast of Cornwall | In the middle of a desert | *In eastern England | In the mountains of Wales
exercise: In the made-up language Selk, «fenmor» means a volcano. Does fen mean fire in English? | Only in summer | Yes, always | *No, in English a fen is low, wet land | Yes, but only in Scotland
test: Much of the Fens was drained so that | people could build tall mountains | *farmers could grow crops | the water could freeze into ice | the reeds could grow taller
test: Which word best describes a fen? | Hot and dusty | Tall and steep | Dry and rocky | *Wet and flat
exam: A fen is best described as | a busy city street | *a low, flat, wet area like a marsh | a dry hill with lots of trees | a steep mountain with snow on top
